e.\" Process this file with
.\" groff -man -Tascii sgml2lyx.1
.\"
.TH SGML2LYX 1 "2025-04-06"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
sgml2lyx \- create LyX output from a LinuxDoc DTD SGML source file
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.B sgml2lyx [generic-option...]
.IR file [.sgml]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.B sgml2lyx
is an old and obsoleted form of the lyx converter command
of LinuxDoc-Tools
(its name may be misleading, as it is not a tool for any SGML DTD, only
supports the SGML LinuxDoc DTD).
It is recommended to switch the new form
.B linuxdoc -B lyx
now.
It converts a LinuxDoc DTD SGML source file to LyX output.
Output will appear in
.I file.lyx
where
.I file
is the name of the SGML source file.
.LP
The attribute/value pair "output=lyx" is set for conditionals.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.B sgm2lyx
accepts all the generic options described in
.BR linuxdoc (1).
.IP file
The SGML source file, named either
.I file
or
.I file.sgml
.SH "فایل‌ها (FILES)"
Many files and executables in /usr/share/linuxdoc-tools and /usr/bin are used.
.SH "اشکالات (BUGS)"
None known.
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
Originally written by Frank Pavageau <frank@via.ecp.fr> and
Cees de Groot <cg@cdegroot.com> as sgml2lyx and maintained by
Taketoshi Sano <sano@debian.org> for Linuxdoc-Tools.
Currently maintained by Agustin Martin <agustin6martin AT gmail com>.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.BR linuxdoc (1),
.BR sgml2html (1),
.BR sgml2info (1),
.BR sgml2latex (1),
.BR sgml2rtf (1),
.BR sgml2txt (1),
.BR sgmlcheck (1).
